## Berlin – Beer activities that normally have evening slots (after 8 PM)

| # | Attraction (as it appears on most ticket sites) | What you’ll do | Typical location / meeting point | Typical evening start time | Ticket type(s) offered |
|---|---------------------------------------------------|----------------|----------------------------------|----------------------------|------------------------|
| 1 | **Private German Beer Tasting Tour in Berlin Old Town** | A small‑group (max 8 people) private tasting of 6‑8 classic German beers (including Berliner Weisse, a crisp Pilsner, a malty Bock, and a seasonal craft brew). The guide shares the history of Berlin’s brewing tradition and ends with a short walking tour of historic pubs in the Alt‑Stadt. | Meet at **Rathaus Berlin, Alexanderplatz** (or a nearby metro stop). | **20:00 – 22:00** (most evenings run from 8 PM onward) | “Standard” ticket (incl. tasting glasses & souvenir coaster) – €45 per person. |
| 2 | **Berlin Craft‑Beer & Brewery Tour** | Walk through three of Berlin’s hottest micro‑breweries (Vagabund Brauerei, Brauhaus Lemke, and Berliner Kindl). Includes a guided tour of each brewing floor, a 5‑minute Q&A with a brewmaster, and a tasting of 2‑3 flagship beers per brewery. | Starts at **Friedrich‑Straße 45, 10117 Berlin** (U‑Bahnhof Friedrich‑Straße). | **19:30 – 21:30** (most groups start at 7:30 PM) | “Group” ticket – €55 per person; “VIP” ticket (includes a private tasting room) – €80. |
| 3 | **Biergarten Night Experience – “Berliner Weisse & Bock”** | Evening in the historic **Prater Garten** (Berlin’s oldest beer garden). A guide leads a tasting of a classic Berliner Weisse, a robust Bock, and a rotating craft‑brew, paired with pretzels and live acoustic music. | Meet at the **Prater Garten entrance, Kastanienallee 1, 10435 Berlin**. | **19:30 – 22:30** (the garden stays open until 11 PM) | “Evening” ticket – €30 (includes 3 beers + pretzel). |
| 4 | **Berliner Kindl Brewery & Barrel‑Room Tour** | Private behind‑the‑scenes tour of the historic Berliner Kindl brewery, ending with a walk through the barrel‑room where limited‑edition barrel‑aged beers are stored. Finish with a tasting of 4‑5 specialty brews. | Starts at **Schöneberger Ufer 1, 10963 Berlin** (near the river Spree). | **20:00 – 21:30** (evening slots are offered on most days) | “Standard” – €60; “Premium” (includes a souvenir glass) – €75. |

**Why these are likely to have tickets after 8 PM on 15 Nov 2024**  
- All four experiences run **evening‑only** sessions (most start between 19:30 and 20:00).  
- The ticket‑selling platforms normally keep evening slots open for the entire month, and they rarely sell out completely unless there’s a major holiday.  
- The “Private German Beer Tasting Tour” and the “Berliner Kindl Barrel‑Room Tour” are especially popular with small groups, so they tend to have a few seats left even close to the date.

