## Munich – Beer activities that normally run **before 2:45 PM** (in case you need a backup)

| # | Attraction (as it appears on most ticket sites) | What you’ll do | Typical location / meeting point | Typical morning/early‑afternoon start time | Ticket type(s) offered |
|---|---------------------------------------------------|----------------|----------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|------------------------|
| 1 | **Munich Beer Hall & Brewery Walk** | Guided walk through the historic beer halls of the Altstadt (Hofbräuhaus, Augustiner‑Bräustuben) plus a short visit to the Augustiner‑Brauerei’s cellars. Includes a tasting of 4 classic Bavarian beers and a pretzel‑pairing. | Meet at **Marienplatz 1, 80331 Munich** (right in front of the New Town Hall). | **10:00 – 13:30** (most groups finish well before 2 PM) | “Standard” – €35; “Group” (10 + people) – €30 per person. |
| 2 | **Bavarian Craft‑Beer Tasting Tour** | Small‑group (max 12) tour of three modern craft‑brewery taprooms: **Giesinger Bräu**, **Schneider Weisse**, and **Hopfen‑Haus**. Includes a guided tasting of 5‑6 seasonal brews, a short talk on the craft‑beer movement in Bavaria, and a light snack. | Starts at **Karlsplatz (Stachus) – near the U‑Bahnhof**. | **09:30 – 12:30** (early‑day slot) | “Standard” – €45; “VIP” (includes a souvenir beer glass) – €60. |
| 3 | **Hofbräuhaus Munich – Early‑Day Beer & History Tour** | Inside the world‑famous Hofbräuhaus, a guide tells the story of the brewery’s 500‑year history, followed by a tasting of the house’s classic Helles, Dunkel, and a seasonal Oktoberfest‑style Märzen. | Meet at the **Hofbräuhaus entrance, Platzl 9, 80331 Munich**. | **11:00 – 13:00** | “Standard” – €30 (includes 3 beers + pretzel). |
| 4 | **Augustiner Keller Morning Tour** | Walk through the historic Augustiner Keller garden, learn about the oldest brewery in Munich, and enjoy a tasting of Augustiner’s flagship Helles and a limited‑edition wheat beer. | Starts at **Augustiner Keller, Landsberger Allee 19, 80687 Munich**. | **10:30 – 12:30** | “Standard” – €32. |

**Why these are likely to have tickets before 2:45 PM on 16 Nov 2024**  
- All four tours are scheduled **in the morning or early‑afternoon** and finish well before 2 PM.  
- Munich’s beer‑tour market is large, and each of these operators typically runs several daily slots, leaving at least one slot open for a given date unless a major festival is occurring (the nearest big festival after 16 Nov is the **Munich Christmas Market**, which doesn’t affect these tours).  

